Package: statarbor
Title: Assumption-Guided Statistical Engine and Bilingual Reporting
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Taha",
           family = "BAŞTUĞ",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "tahabastug@protonmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2382-6302"))
Description: Provides an assumption-guided statistical decision engine for
    biological, agricultural, and experimental datasets. Automatically evaluates
    normality, homoscedasticity, overdispersion, slope homogeneity, and
    zero-variance edge cases to route analyses across independent multi-group
    comparisons (ANOVA/Tukey, Welch/Games-Howell, Kruskal-Wallis/Dunn), paired
    and repeated-measures designs (paired t/Wilcoxon, Greenhouse-Geisser
    RM-ANOVA/Friedman), count regressions (Poisson/Negative Binomial with
    Hauck-Donner safeguards), ANCOVA, randomized complete block designs (RCBD),
    Firth logistic regression, ordinal cumulative link models, and factorial
    GLMs. Generates special-character-safe compact letter displays (CLD), effect
    sizes, reproducible R scripts, bilingual (English/Turkish) methods
    paragraphs, formatted 'Word' reports, and an interactive 'Shiny' interface.
